WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:01.729
Henry: Hi!

00:00:01.729 --> 00:00:06.690
John: Hi! Happy birthday, Uncle Hank! He’s
not gonna say that, he’s just gonna say

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.690
hi.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:08.690
Henry: Hi.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.219
John: Good morning Hank it’s Thursday, May
5th, 2011; you are 31 years old! It’s Hanko

00:00:12.219 --> 00:00:13.219
de Mayo!

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:17.279
So Hank, in the video responses below you’ll
find many amazing birthday wishes from Nerdfighteria.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:21.240
I’ll be tweeting and reblogging those all
day. Also for your birthday I taught Henry

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.240
your name.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.240
Henry: Hank!

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.930
John: And today you will also be receiving
a large box full of birthday greetings from

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.210
Nerdfighters all over the world that were
mailed to a P.O. box in Ohio. That P.O. box

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.440
is maintained by the nerdfightastic Valerie2776,
the two thousand seven hundred and seventy-sixth

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.210
Valerie to enter the internet, but the first
in our hearts.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.079
Hank, in a few of those cards you’ll find
a dollar or two. We would like to challenge

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:46.420
you to pool that money and spend it in the
way that, in your opinion, most increases

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.960
awesome. So we look forward to seeing what
you do with that.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.130
?And Nerdfighters, if you still want to send
Hank a belated birthday card, that is possible;

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.109
just mail it to the P.O. box in the doobly-doo.

00:00:54.109 --> 00:00:57.629
And lastly, Hank, as previously noted, it
is Thursday. I chose not to upload a video

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:02.399
yesterday because I figured that the greatest
gift I can give my brother is the opportunity

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:08.730
to force me to do something humiliating and/or
embarrassing and/or unpalatable. So Nerdfighters,

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.940
leave your punishment suggestions in comments,
and Hank, when you are choosing a punishment,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.100
I ask only that you not think of the brother
who tried to poison you to death with iodine

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.480
when you were an infant or the brother who
repeatedly stole from your piggy bank when

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:23.210
you were a child, but the brother with whom
you have been making YouTube videos lo these

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.210
many years.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.750
Alright, Hank, so you’re 31 today. Since
you turned 30, you have continued to publish

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.600
EcoGeek.org, the best environmental technology
website on the internet. And you fostered

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.990
the career of young musicians from Chameleon
Circuit to Mike Lombardo through your work

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:38.980
at DFTBA Records. In the last year you also
organized and ran VidCon, the largest online

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.330
video conference in the world. Frustrated
with the increasing three-dimensionality of

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.960
the screens we look at precisely so we can
avoid looking at the actual three-dimensional

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.940
world, you invented 2D glasses. You also oversaw
the 2010 Project for Awesome which raised

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:56.590
more than $150,000 for charity, and you wrote
songs about making babies and Phineas Gage

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.320
and the fundamental constituent of matter
observed in 1968 through deep electric scatter.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.790
In the last year you made more than 100 videos
that we watched more than ten million times;

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.390
you inspired us to support the building of
a well by traveling to Haiti with Water.org.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:10.420
You created Your Pants more or less overnight
- things that don’t make sense to new viewers!

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:13.819
And you built Phototrometon and the HankGames
YouTube channel and you ran Truth or Fail

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:17.920
and you donated blood twice and two days ago,
you beat Portal 2!

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.650
Hank, that’s a good year. And while I know
you’d hasten to say that none of this could

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:26.189
be done without Nerdfighteria, and that’s
true, just like you need us, we need you,

00:02:26.189 --> 00:02:27.189
so thank you.

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:30.160
And Hank, not to quote a quote I stole from
my wife and used in my first novel, but while

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.200
I understand that imagining the future is
a kind of nostalgia, I still can’t wait

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:40.319
to see what you do with 31. Hank, thank you
for being awesome, best wishes, happy Hanko

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:45.709
de Mayo! I will see you tomorrow! ...is something
I haven’t been able to say in a long time!

